[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"ORM Concepts and Hibernate Architecture Tutorial"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Object-Relational Mapping (ORM) is a programming technique used to convert data between incompatible type systems in object-oriented programming languages and relational databases. Hibernate is one of the most popular ORM frameworks for Java, providing a powerful abstraction layer over JDBC."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Core ORM Concepts"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Mapping Entities: Java classes are mapped directly to database tables, where class attributes correspond to table columns."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Association Mapping: Relationships such as One-to-One, One-to-Many, and Many-to-Many are represented using object references rather than foreign keys."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Identity and State: Hibernate tracks entity states across the application lifecycle, moving between Transient, Persistent, and Detached states."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Hibernate Architecture Overview"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Hibernate architecture integrates the database, Java application, and configuration data. It consists of several key interfaces and layers that manage persistence operations."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Configuration (Configuration): A one-time setup object used to gather mapping documents and property settings to create a SessionFactory."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"SessionFactory: A heavy-weight, thread-safe factory object that creates Session instances for the entire application."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Session: A light-weight, non-thread-safe interface representing a single unit of work between the Java application and the database."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Transaction: Manages database transactions, ensuring ACID properties for a series of operations."},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Code Example: Basic Hibernate Configuration"},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"Configuration config = new Configuration();
config.configure("hibernate.cfg.xml");
config.addAnnotatedClass(User.class);
SessionFactory factory = config.buildSessionFactory();
Session session = factory.openSession();"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"By leveraging Hibernate and ORM concepts, developers can reduce boilerplate database code, maintain cleaner domain models, and write database-agnostic applications."}]
